[15:30:51Z] :: igpu-blt: ring=absent why=no-active-surface — every iGPU display plane is off (gmux routes the panel elsewhere); CPU path carries the console ::
[15:30:51Z] :: igpu: [CITATION: Intel PRM Vol 3, Display Registers] On Ivy Bridge (Gen7 / Panther Point 7-Series PCH), the Display Engine is split.
[15:30:51Z] :: igpu: [CITATION: Intel PRM Vol 3, Display Registers, Section 1.1.2] eDP on Port A (DP_A) is CPU-attached (North Display Engine).
[15:30:51Z] :: igpu: [CITATION: Intel PRM Vol 3, South Display Engine Registers] GMBUS and Panel Power Sequencer (PPS) are PCH-attached (South Display Engine).
[15:30:51Z] :: igpu: [CITATION: Intel PRM Vol 3, South Display Engine Registers] Therefore, GMBUS is at PCH base 0xC5100 and PPS is at PCH base 0xC7200.
[15:30:51Z] :: igpu: [CITATION: Intel PRM Vol 3, Display Registers] Because eDP is CPU-attached, the FDI link (CPU-to-PCH) is bypassed for the internal panel.
